---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import benMayer from '../assets/about/ben-mayer.jpg';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Ben Mayer - Product Manager and developer, currently in Berlin."
>
  <div class="container about-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </section>
    <Image src={benMayer} alt="Picture of Ben Mayer" width={400} height={400} />
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I love building products, have for 20 odd years.</p>
      <p>
        It started with a MySpace page. I wanted my band's to stand out and couldn't
        afford to pay anyone to do it. So I sat down and taught myself. I was hooked. I
        spent hours at night tinkering with HTML and CSS to build the perfect MySpace
        page, and later combined learning Photoshop, Illustrator with Adobe Flash and
        ActionScript to create an even better website. (We got very lucky Flash websites
        didn't catch on).
      </p>
      <p>
        At uni other fellow musicians started asking. That led me to launch a web design
        and social media agency for musicians in 2012. The portfolio got me into EMI and
        later Universal Music, where I built sites and stores for The Beatles, Coldplay,
        Blur, Oasis and Lady Gaga.
      </p>
      <p>
        Quite randomly in 2015, I moved across the world to join two founders running a
        digital ad agency in Sydney. My ideas for automating their manual work turned the
        agency into a B2B AdTech SaaS company. It won the Digital Advertising Awards APAC
        in 2019, the year after I left, and it's still one of the projects I'm most proud
        of.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the years since I've launched and iterated over mobile consumer subscription
        products for several million users globally at Marley Spoon and 7Mind, and led a
        team of 20 at Urban Sports Club.
      </p>
      <p>
        Right now I'm back to building things myself. Join In is a peer matching app for
        people who train alone and would rather not, and for groups who are a player
        short. Working with AI tools has fundamentally changed how we build digital
        products. Now the loop from idea to shipped product is shorter than ever. It's
        the most fun I've had in about a decade.
      </p>
      <p>
        Aside from all that, I love being active. I can't go for long without going
        surfing, rock climbing or skating. I live in Berlin, mostly, sometimes in Spain or
        Asia and work remote.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-links">
      <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/benlmayer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
      <a href="http://github.com/benmayer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-page {
    max-width: 42rem;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 0 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  .about-page img {
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem auto;
  }

  .about-links {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
</style>
